<title>KENYA: Coffee scientists to meet in Nairobi July 20-25.</title>
<headline>Coffee scientists to meet in Nairobi July 20-25.</headline>
<dateline>NAIROBI 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Conference on Coffee Science (ASIC) will hold its 17th congress in Kenya July 20 to 25, focusing on improved quality, organisers said.</p>
<p>Coffee researcher and consultant Wilson Opile told Reuters on Wednesday that the scientists would be looking at the transfer of technology to boost coffee quality.</p>
<p>&quot;The main aim is the improvement of coffee quality in the mutual interest of producers, traders, industrialists and consumers,&quot; said Opile, who retired as chief researcher and director of Kenya's Coffee Research Foundation in October.</p>
<p>--Nairobi Newsroom ++254-2 330-261.</p>
